WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.850
The Marvel Cinematic Universe isn't done with
the Avengers — but that doesn't mean that

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.600
fans should expect more of the same.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:13.160
Speaking with MTV News at San Diego Comic-Con
2019, studio boss Kevin Feige revealed that

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:18.470
Mighty Marvel indeed has plans for its flagship
superhero team moving forward — but that

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:21.820
said team will look quite a bit different
from what we're used to.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:26.540
This shouldn't come as too big of a shock,
because in terms of brand recognition, the

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.220
Avengers name is without equal in the world
of mainstream film.

00:00:30.409 --> 00:00:34.940
Each of the four films that have been released
so far with that word in the title have grossed

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.020
over a billion dollars at the worldwide box
office.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:44.600
The Infinity Saga-culminating Avengers: Endgame
even became the all-time box office champion,

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.980
surpassing the decade-old record previously
held by James Cameron's Avatar.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:54.460
"Magnificent!

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.100
Magnificent!

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.260
MAGNIFICENT!"

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.500
According to Feige, a new iteration of the
Avengers is on the horizon — but it's not

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.200
likely to feature many, if any, revamped versions
of heroes we're familiar with.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:13.680
The King Geek was asked point-blank by MTV
News if he and the rest of the Marvel Studios

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.780
brain trust know what the next Avengers team
will look like, and he replied, "Yes."

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.270
After a lengthy pause, Feige continued,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.060
"It will be a very different team than what
we've seen before, that's what Endgame was

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:26.880
all about.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.280
It will be a very different incarnation of
the team, with some people you've already

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.860
met, and some people you haven't met yet."

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:39.200
Whatever form this team eventually takes,
it seems safe to say that we won't see another

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.920
proper Avengers film for quite some time,
considering that the entirety of Marvel's

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:49.119
Phase 4 slate was announced during the studio's
rapturously received Comic-Con panel — and

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.960
there was nary a giant team-up flick to be
found.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:56.970
There may be a few clues, however, hidden
in the details we know so far about Phase

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:57.960
4 and beyond.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:02.500
First, it's been revealed that two prominent
characters will be getting their introductions

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:07.909
by way of standalone solo flicks in the coming
years — one during Phase 4, and one during

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:08.700
Phase 5.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.520
February 12th, 2021, will see the release
of Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings,

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:19.360
which will introduce audiences worldwide to
the legendary Master of Kung Fu — along

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.740
with… drumroll please! … the actual Mandarin!

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:24.040
"You want something?

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:24.720
Take it!

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.640
Although, the guns are all fake because the
w***ers wouldn't trust me with the real ones."

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:28.140
"What?"

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.660
We said the actual Mandarin!

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.240
Get outta here, Trevor!

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:32.980
Anyway…

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:37.700
Marvel hopes that the flick — with its mostly
Asian cast and behind-the-camera talent — will

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:42.360
be the kind of paradigm-shifting event that
2018's Black Panther proved to be, and if

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.920
this works out like we all know it probably
will, the character would be a fine inclusion

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.500
in team-up films in the future.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:53.920
In the comics, Shang-Chi — although he has
no superpowers for most of his heroic career

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:59.640
— is among the finest unarmed combatants
in existence, more than capable of going toe-to-toe

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.080
with superpowered opponents.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.950
Phase 5 will bring us the solo vehicle for
that deadly, smack-talking half human-half

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:10.690
vampire Blade, who was portrayed by Wesley
Snipes in the successful film trilogy of the

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.640
late '90s and early 2000s.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:18.420
In the MCU, the "daywalker" will be played
by two-time Oscar winner Mahershala Ali, and

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:22.300
it seems unlikely that Marvel would cast an
actor of that caliber without having some

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.300
pretty big plans for the future.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.940
Save for those two additions to some potential
super squad… well, who knows?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.420
Feige suggested to MTV News that, though there
may never be another culmination of a decade-long

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:39.020
arc like Endgame, that doesn't mean that the
future of the MCU won't play host to some

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:40.080
thrilling events.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:41.200
He elaborated:

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:44.800
"That's what I love about the Marvel comic
method of storytelling.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:50.620
I love things that build up, they build to
a crescendo, they all get together, they separate,

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:51.280
they change.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:57.120
And now that we get to do that, not just in
movies but on these mega-event series on Disney+,

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:00.660
it's just invigorated all of us at Marvel
Studios to keep going."

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:05.980
Feige and company certainly haven't steered
us wrong so far, and like you, we can't wait

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:08.140
to see what they have in store for us in the
years ahead.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:12.370
It'll be interesting to see whether Marvel
can make household names out of some relatively

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:17.430
lesser-known characters yet again — which
is almost certainly the plan, and we wouldn't

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:18.320
bet against them.

